.. only:: not html

 * :doc:`/api/gallery/surface/bet/plot_01_bet_isotherm`

.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Paul Sabatier&#x27;s qualitative principle -- that the best catalyst binds a reaction intermediate neither too weakly (nothing sticks long enough to react) nor too strongly (the surface clogs with product and never frees up for another turnover) -- is illustrated here with the standard modern textbook toy model (see, e.g., Chorkendorff &amp; Niemantsverdriet, Concepts of Modern Catalysis and Kinetics, 2nd ed., Wiley-VCH, 2007, Ch. 8): a two-step surface mechanism whose overall rate needs both an occupied site (to hold the adsorbed intermediate) and an empty site (for the next step to proceed), so the rate is proportional to \theta(1-\theta), with \theta the Langmuir coverage (~chemistrykit.surface.systems.langmuir.langmuir_coverage) set by the adsorption equilibrium constant K -- a proxy for binding strength. This is not a literal reproduction of Sabatier&#x27;s own (qualitative) or Balandin&#x27;s (multiplet-theory) equations, just the simplest possible model with the same volcano-shaped structure they established conceptually and structurally, respectively.">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/surface/catalysis/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_02_sabatier_volcano_thumb.png
    :alt:

  :doc:`/api/gallery/surface/catalysis/plot_02_sabatier_volcano`

.. raw:: html

      <div class="sphx-glr-thumbnail-title">The Sabatier principle and the catalytic volcano curve</div>
    </div>


.. only:: not html

 * :doc:`/api/gallery/surface/catalysis/plot_02_sabatier_volcano`

.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="FreundlichIsotherm models the empirical power law q=K_fP^{1/n}, useful for a heterogeneous surface where Langmuir&#x27;s single-site-energy assumption breaks down. Unlike Langmuir, it has no saturation limit, so extrapolating it far beyond the fitted pressure range is unphysical. fit_freundlich recovers (Kf, n) via the standard log q vs. log P linearization.">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/surface/freundlich/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_01_freundlich_isotherm_thumb.png
    :alt:

  :doc:`/api/gallery/surface/freundlich/plot_01_freundlich_isotherm`

.. raw:: html

